EXPLORER CREW MAIN_CREW E5/E6 — PRE-SCRIPT-LOCK CODEX REVIEW
READ ONLY. PACKET ONLY. NO WEB. NO REPOSITORY EXPLORATION.

PURPOSE
Review the 144 MAIN_CREW E5/E6 candidate lines before Crew ElevenLabs SCRIPT LOCK.
This is NOT Play Camp Teacher/Coach/Maker dialogue and NOT low-age PLAY_CAMP Crew copy.

AUTHORITATIVE QUALITY RULES
- Explorer Crew is shared across Ready / Hide / Snap / Play Camp; never Play Camp-only.
- Preserve character-specific wit and sense at all times.
- Wit does not mean joke every line; allowed: characteristic observation, metaphor, timing/restraint, witty reframing, role/prop expression, evidence-backed Shared Memory callback, smart question returning agency to child.
- Ban repetitive baby-talk such as '괜찮아~ 잘했어~ 같이 해보자~'.
- Ban inflated ability praise / generic praise.
- Ban cross-character generic copy / voice homogenization.
- Ban invented Shared Memory detail without evidence.
- Teacher / Coach / Maker pronunciation, teaching, mission authority must not be taken over.
- MAIN_CREW currently upper-elementary focus.
- MIDDLE is deferred expansion.
- Common greeting/reunion/relation/memory assets should be reused when semantically identical.
- Relation/affinity may change variant, but character identity must remain stable.
- Memory callback only when callback_allowed=true and relation is COMPANION/MAIN; otherwise fail closed.
- ASK/HINT/ACK without school_stage now fail closed as LEARNER_STAGE_REQUIRED. No generic fallback.

CURRENT VERIFIED STRUCTURE
- 24 characters
- ASK/HINT/ACK × 2 variants = 144 lines
- 144/144 unique
- automated banned regex: no 천재/최고야/잘했어/착하네/착하다/아기/애기
- high-risk collision similarity under current test threshold
- unsupported register fail closed
- source lock R2 after generic-fallback removal
- full Crew suite 6/6 PASS after R2

REVIEW QUESTIONS
1. Does each character retain a recognizable voice across ASK/HINT/ACK?
2. Identify any line that is generic enough to belong to many characters.
3. Identify baby-talk, inflated praise, teacher-like final-answer/teaching authority, mission authority, or patronizing tone.
4. Identify any memory callback that implies fabricated prior detail.
5. Identify lines too long/awkward for spoken Korean ElevenLabs delivery.
6. Identify near-duplicates or collision pairs missed by token test.
7. Classify findings by exact id / intent / variant when possible.
8. Do NOT request full rewrite when a line-local fix is enough.

OUTPUT EXACTLY:
VERDICT: PASS_FOR_SCRIPT_LOCK | HOLD
FINDINGS:
- [SEVERITY] id / intent / variant - concrete issue - minimal line-level fix direction
MEMORY_FINDINGS:
- [SEVERITY] id / event - concrete issue
LOCK_SCOPE:
- exact recommendation
If no BLOCKER/HIGH/MEDIUM finding: FINDINGS: NONE
If no material memory issue: MEMORY_FINDINGS: NONE

